WEBVTT

00:00:11.510 --> 00:00:12.850
Here...

00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:22.250
Team Foo Fighter... This 
is where I'll get strong.

00:00:40.250 --> 00:00:43.560
Um... Are you waiting for someone?

00:00:43.940 --> 00:00:47.440
My name isn't "Waiting for Someone".

00:00:47.780 --> 00:00:49.880
No, I didn't mean that...

00:00:50.990 --> 00:00:53.650
It's not "I Didn't Mean That" either.

00:00:53.650 --> 00:00:56.960
Jeez... What's with this guy?

00:01:00.110 --> 00:01:03.360
Are you a Cardfighter, too?

00:01:03.360 --> 00:01:06.040
Yes, I'm a Cardfighter, too.

00:01:06.040 --> 00:01:08.470
Oh...

00:01:08.650 --> 00:01:12.480
He must have been scouted 
from somewhere, too.

00:01:13.360 --> 00:01:16.660
So, why are you standing here?

00:01:16.660 --> 00:01:18.130
Instead of going in...

00:01:18.130 --> 00:01:20.160
The door won't open.

00:01:20.840 --> 00:01:24.740
It always opens like "whirrr" 
when I stand here...

00:01:24.740 --> 00:01:26.940
Um... The door is here.

00:01:26.940 --> 00:01:30.640
I get it! The entrance is over there!

00:01:32.270 --> 00:01:35.490
Was he really scouted?

00:01:35.490 --> 00:01:38.320
He doesn't seem like much of a fighter...

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:44.290
I've been waiting for you, Ren.

00:01:44.720 --> 00:01:46.050
You're late.

00:01:46.050 --> 00:01:51.000
Yeah. And I would've been 
later if I hadn't met her.

00:01:54.930 --> 00:01:57.500
Asaka Narumi, I presume?

00:01:57.790 --> 00:01:59.930
Y-Yes!

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:02.360
Um... Who is he?

00:03:33.640 --> 00:03:36.180
Um... Who is he?

00:03:36.180 --> 00:03:42.170
Ren Suzugamori. He's the commander-in-chief 
of Foo Fighter. Our leader.

00:03:43.010 --> 00:03:44.570
Leader?!

00:03:49.170 --> 00:03:51.990
All right, everyone is all fired up!

00:03:51.990 --> 00:03:55.500
We're here at the final round of 
the Vanguard National Championship!

00:03:55.770 --> 00:04:00.950
In the first battle, Tetsu Shinjou 
beat Kamui Katsuragi by a whisker,

00:04:00.950 --> 00:04:06.050
making one win for Foo Fighter AL4!

00:04:06.050 --> 00:04:09.680
It was a spectacular fight, wasn't it?

00:04:09.950 --> 00:04:15.370
Our second match is between 
Asaka Narumi and Misaki Tokura.

00:04:15.370 --> 00:04:19.280
If you'll recall, both of these fighters 
faced each other at the last championship.

00:04:19.280 --> 00:04:22.630
Indeed. Last time, Narumi 
was the vict-<i>o</i>-r,

00:04:22.630 --> 00:04:26.900
but what will happen this time 
around? It's s-<i>o</i> exciting!

00:04:28.080 --> 00:04:29.950
It's been a while, huh?

00:04:29.950 --> 00:04:31.120
Yes.

00:04:32.160 --> 00:04:37.170
Last time, she could see two steps 
ahead of me and acted accordingly.

00:04:37.740 --> 00:04:42.640
But my judgment was off and the 
makeup of my deck was poor.

00:04:42.640 --> 00:04:46.390
That was because I was 
woefully short on experience.

00:04:46.720 --> 00:04:48.620
But now it's different.

00:04:48.970 --> 00:04:53.930
After fighting Yuri and others, 
both my deck and I have grown.

00:04:53.930 --> 00:04:55.640
So this time for sure...

00:04:55.950 --> 00:04:59.050
What's the scary look for?

00:04:59.190 --> 00:05:01.510
I'm going to settle the score between us!

00:05:01.510 --> 00:05:04.110
I wonder if you can...

00:05:04.480 --> 00:05:07.530
Let the second match of 
the final round begin!

00:05:07.530 --> 00:05:09.810
Stand up, Vanguard!

00:05:18.960 --> 00:05:21.250
Godhawk, Ichibyoshi!

00:05:21.250 --> 00:05:23.960
Hades Ringmaster!

00:05:28.200 --> 00:05:30.960
So this is a fight you can't lose, eh?

00:05:31.050 --> 00:05:33.370
But it's the same thing for me!

00:05:33.870 --> 00:05:39.210
Ever since that day, I haven't 
been able to afford to lose...

00:05:38.880 --> 00:05:43.890
Feelings Towards Foo Fighter

00:05:46.400 --> 00:05:50.370
First let's see what you've 
got, Asaka Narumi.

00:05:50.370 --> 00:05:54.540
S-Sure. Will I be playing against you?

00:05:54.920 --> 00:05:58.870
No. One more fighter has 
joined the team today.

00:05:58.950 --> 00:06:01.540
We'll start by pitting you two 
newbies against each other.

00:06:02.110 --> 00:06:04.380
Yeesh. He's just a child...

00:06:04.810 --> 00:06:08.260
Hey, you're looking down on me, aren't you?!

00:06:08.520 --> 00:06:10.800
Huh? I didn't say anything...

00:06:10.800 --> 00:06:14.240
Heh! I'm the one who should be complaining!

00:06:14.240 --> 00:06:18.080
I only came because I heard they're 
gathering strong fighters from around the country!

00:06:18.080 --> 00:06:20.650
But suddenly, they want me to fight a woman?

00:06:20.890 --> 00:06:23.260
What difference does me being a woman make?!

00:06:23.260 --> 00:06:25.590
I was scouted, too!

00:06:25.590 --> 00:06:28.040
And I'm not gonna lose against some kid!

00:06:28.040 --> 00:06:31.660
I'll remember that. Just don't expect 
sympathy if you're crying later!

00:06:32.360 --> 00:06:34.040
Right back at you!

00:06:41.260 --> 00:06:43.840
Stand up, Vanguard!

00:06:47.230 --> 00:06:51.800
Ren, why did you summon a fighter like that?

00:06:52.680 --> 00:06:54.190
What do you mean?

00:06:54.190 --> 00:06:55.950
Asaka Narumi...

00:06:55.950 --> 00:06:57.430
That woman isn't ready yet.

00:06:57.700 --> 00:07:00.140
But she seems interesting, doesn't she?

00:07:00.600 --> 00:07:02.570
And I like those eyes.

00:07:06.970 --> 00:07:11.230
Her unyielding spirit hasn't 
changed a bit since then...

00:07:17.480 --> 00:07:19.710
Here I go. Draw!

00:07:19.710 --> 00:07:22.530
I activate Godhawk, Ichibyoshi's skill.

00:07:22.560 --> 00:07:25.460
I get to check the top five cards of my deck.

00:07:27.590 --> 00:07:31.860
I superior ride Goddess of 
the Crescent Moon, Tsukuyomi!

00:07:37.370 --> 00:07:40.930
All right! She starts by riding 
Goddess of the Crescent Moon!

00:07:40.930 --> 00:07:42.800
That's a good start!

00:07:42.930 --> 00:07:44.230
Turn end.

00:07:44.740 --> 00:07:48.960
From New Moon to Crescent 
Moon... and then Full Moon?

00:07:49.050 --> 00:07:51.300
This fight is the same as our last one.

00:07:51.550 --> 00:07:53.330
But that works for me.

00:07:53.560 --> 00:08:00.200
I can't lose face in front of Ren... 
like that time... ever again.

00:08:00.200 --> 00:08:05.150
I attack with Juggernaut 
Maximum, and Soulblast!

00:08:05.150 --> 00:08:06.950
+5000 power!

00:08:06.950 --> 00:08:09.120
Including the boost from Wonder Boy,

00:08:09.120 --> 00:08:11.840
that's a 24000 attack!

00:08:18.670 --> 00:08:20.970
That was nothin'!

00:08:21.340 --> 00:08:25.190
You lost to a little kid.

00:08:25.190 --> 00:08:29.970
Man... I wonder why they even 
scouted somebody like you!

00:08:29.970 --> 00:08:33.100
Maybe it was a clerical error!

00:08:35.970 --> 00:08:39.910
Pale Moon deck. That's an interesting one.

00:08:41.270 --> 00:08:45.710
The deck is like a, what... like a circus.

00:08:45.710 --> 00:08:49.350
You could call it the Pale Moon Circus...

00:08:51.480 --> 00:08:55.570
Can I see that deck?

00:08:55.570 --> 00:08:57.000
Ren...

00:08:57.000 --> 00:09:00.560
What's the harm? No need to be so formal...

00:09:02.190 --> 00:09:05.380
Huh! I see...

00:09:05.380 --> 00:09:08.900
H-Hey! I'm the one who won!

00:09:08.900 --> 00:09:11.560
Oh, that's right.

00:09:11.560 --> 00:09:14.830
But I'm not interested in your deck.

00:09:15.930 --> 00:09:18.390
That deck is well put together.

00:09:18.390 --> 00:09:20.640
In other words, it's completed.

00:09:20.640 --> 00:09:23.500
As such, it's not interesting.

00:09:23.500 --> 00:09:26.270
Why, you... Ren!

00:09:26.900 --> 00:09:30.620
Treat Ren with respect, newbie.

00:09:35.220 --> 00:09:36.740
Thank you.

00:09:37.170 --> 00:09:39.240
Ren... sir...

00:09:41.160 --> 00:09:44.360
As I thought, it's an interesting deck.

00:09:44.360 --> 00:09:48.140
But as it stands, the 
circus tent won't go up.

00:09:50.300 --> 00:09:54.610
He's saying that you need 
to improve your deck.

00:09:55.360 --> 00:09:58.680
Improve it? How?

00:09:58.720 --> 00:10:01.300
That's something you need 
to think about yourself.

00:10:04.360 --> 00:10:07.640
And then, once you perfect the deck,

00:10:07.640 --> 00:10:11.180
I'm sure you'll become a member of AL4.

00:10:11.570 --> 00:10:13.350
AL4?

00:10:13.350 --> 00:10:15.730
Apex Limited 4.

00:10:15.730 --> 00:10:20.110
The strongest team of all, comprised 
of the top four members of Foo Fighter.

00:10:20.110 --> 00:10:22.340
I'll be able to join the strongest team?!

00:10:22.340 --> 00:10:25.140
That's only if you show us strength 
commensurate with that level.

00:10:25.140 --> 00:10:28.550
W-Wait a second! What, am 
I cast out in the cold?!

00:10:28.550 --> 00:10:34.180
No. Ren is the only set member of AL4.

00:10:36.180 --> 00:10:39.400
You have a chance to fill one of the 
remaining three positions, depending on your ability.

00:10:39.810 --> 00:10:43.560
Although I'm sure to be one of them.

00:10:43.560 --> 00:10:46.850
Then, two more slots...

00:10:50.160 --> 00:10:55.630
If you want to join AL4, you'll have to 
survive the fights that are held here.

00:11:04.310 --> 00:11:06.250
I have high hopes for you.

00:11:06.750 --> 00:11:09.280
I don't need your lip service to make it!

00:11:09.280 --> 00:11:10.630
You know,

00:11:10.630 --> 00:11:13.560
you're the ringmaster 
of a fascinating circus.

00:11:13.560 --> 00:11:14.420
Yes!

00:11:16.710 --> 00:11:21.830
Ever since then, I've been fighting only for Ren.

00:11:22.220 --> 00:11:23.370
That's why...

00:11:24.520 --> 00:11:26.700
I can't lose!

00:11:30.650 --> 00:11:36.090
Tonight, let's raise the tent again 
of the bewitching Pale Moon Circus!

00:11:39.330 --> 00:11:42.050
I hope you'll enjoy my plethora of tricks

00:11:42.050 --> 00:11:44.630
that are graceful, yet ruthless!

00:11:44.640 --> 00:11:46.600
I ride Midnight Bunny!

00:11:50.520 --> 00:11:53.250
As always, an overblown performance...

00:11:53.820 --> 00:11:58.020
I Soulcharge with the 
skill of Hades Ringmaster!

00:11:58.190 --> 00:11:59.710
Let's go, Bunny!

00:11:59.830 --> 00:12:01.780
Show her a magnificent attack!

00:12:03.770 --> 00:12:04.950
No guard!

00:12:05.040 --> 00:12:06.200
Drive check.

00:12:10.810 --> 00:12:17.070
And thus ends the first act of my circus.

00:12:37.830 --> 00:12:39.840
I stand and draw.

00:12:40.190 --> 00:12:44.560
With the skill of Goddess of the Crescent 
Moon, I check the top five cards.

00:12:47.850 --> 00:12:51.580
She draws five cards and not 
one of them is Half Moon?!

00:12:51.580 --> 00:12:53.680
Well, that happens sometimes!

00:12:53.680 --> 00:12:56.260
No, she must have bad luck today.

00:12:56.260 --> 00:12:58.880
Let's see, her horoscope says...

00:12:58.970 --> 00:13:01.280
What month was she born in again?

00:13:03.330 --> 00:13:06.230
I ride Goddess of the Half Moon, Tsukuyomi!

00:13:10.100 --> 00:13:11.380
Soulcharge!

00:13:12.480 --> 00:13:14.890
I call Battle Maiden, Tagitsuhime!

00:13:17.470 --> 00:13:19.310
I attack with Goddess of the Half Moon!

00:13:19.780 --> 00:13:21.070
No guard.

00:13:21.800 --> 00:13:23.320
Trigger check.

00:13:27.160 --> 00:13:29.190
Damage trigger check.

00:13:29.250 --> 00:13:30.700
I attack with Tagitsuhime!

00:13:37.290 --> 00:13:38.240
Yes!

00:13:38.240 --> 00:13:41.420
Now the damage is 1-2. The tables are turned!

00:13:42.960 --> 00:13:47.860
It's pathetic to be thrilled 
over just a one-point lead.

00:13:47.860 --> 00:13:53.620
A fight like this is nothing when stacked 
up against all of my experience.

00:13:56.130 --> 00:13:59.680
After that first fight, I brought 
all the ability I possessed...

00:13:59.980 --> 00:14:04.440
No, <i>more</i> than the ability I possessed... to 
the fore, and won like my life depended on it.

00:14:06.230 --> 00:14:10.650
Trying to get even a little higher... Trying 
to get even a little closer to Ren...

00:14:11.890 --> 00:14:13.720
And then, at last...

00:14:16.940 --> 00:14:20.340
I finally clawed my way to the top, AL4...

00:14:20.340 --> 00:14:22.290
But I never thought it'd be with you.

00:14:22.570 --> 00:14:24.700
That's my line.

00:14:24.730 --> 00:14:26.430
Also, don't forget.

00:14:26.470 --> 00:14:30.430
I'm third in the team ranking, 
while you're fourth.

00:14:31.640 --> 00:14:33.260
For now...

00:14:33.530 --> 00:14:36.370
Oh. You're going to pass me by someday?

00:14:36.370 --> 00:14:41.180
Of course! I'm gonna be the man 
standing at the top of Foo Fighter!

00:14:41.180 --> 00:14:45.010
Top? Don't tell me you think 
you're going to beat Ren?

00:14:45.010 --> 00:14:46.470
I do!

00:14:46.470 --> 00:14:48.990
Eventually, I'm gonna oust that guy!

00:14:48.990 --> 00:14:51.530
Then Foo Fighter will be mine!

00:14:51.530 --> 00:14:52.780
Kyou!

00:14:53.100 --> 00:14:54.670
Give it up.

00:14:54.670 --> 00:14:58.120
It looks like you've got 
a major crush on Ren,

00:14:58.340 --> 00:15:03.250
but in the end, he's nothing more than a 
little dog chasing after Toshiki Kai's shadow!

00:15:04.250 --> 00:15:06.380
Toshiki... Kai?

00:15:06.380 --> 00:15:09.260
What, you don't know?

00:15:09.690 --> 00:15:11.130
Who is he?

00:15:11.180 --> 00:15:12.800
Don't ask me.

00:15:13.010 --> 00:15:16.100
If you want the answer to that, 
check it out for yourself.

00:15:34.200 --> 00:15:36.810
This is Toshiki Kai?

00:15:40.720 --> 00:15:41.820
Tetsu...

00:15:42.150 --> 00:15:44.440
There's no need for you to know.

00:15:48.970 --> 00:15:52.220
Tell me! You must know something!

00:15:52.220 --> 00:15:55.980
Who is this Kai? What's 
his connection to Ren?!

00:15:57.460 --> 00:16:02.640
He's the one person in the 
world who may beat Ren.

00:16:02.840 --> 00:16:04.290
Beat Ren?!

00:16:04.850 --> 00:16:07.590
He's nothing more nor less than that.

00:16:07.630 --> 00:16:09.090
Are you satisfied?

00:16:10.920 --> 00:16:13.100
Toshiki... Kai...

00:16:21.160 --> 00:16:23.310
Long time no see, eh, Kai?

00:16:26.230 --> 00:16:28.830
I didn't expect to meet you here.

00:16:30.100 --> 00:16:32.050
Why isn't Ren here?

00:16:32.930 --> 00:16:37.670
You really think Ren would bother showing up to 
the preliminary round of the national tournament?

00:16:37.670 --> 00:16:39.430
Even you know better.

00:16:39.430 --> 00:16:43.440
Do I? I've forgotten everything 
that happened back then.

00:16:44.040 --> 00:16:46.230
That's Toshiki Kai...

00:16:46.990 --> 00:16:48.980
So he'll be in the finals.

00:16:49.310 --> 00:16:53.440
You'll probably be able to meet 
him if you make it to the finals.

00:16:53.910 --> 00:16:56.660
I can't lose.

00:16:57.460 --> 00:16:59.560
I have to get strong!

00:16:59.700 --> 00:17:04.290
Stronger! Stronger! So strong 
that Ren will acknowledge me!

00:17:04.290 --> 00:17:06.200
So strong that he'll turn 
around and look at me!

00:17:06.620 --> 00:17:08.870
Strong enough to beat Toshiki Kai...

00:17:11.700 --> 00:17:15.840
That's why I can't stumble here.

00:17:16.510 --> 00:17:21.390
All right! The curtain goes up 
on the second act of my circus!

00:17:21.720 --> 00:17:22.850
Draw!

00:17:23.960 --> 00:17:26.440
I ride Crimson Beast Tamer!

00:17:30.430 --> 00:17:35.680
I call Mirror Demon, Turquoise 
Beast Tamer, and Skull Juggler!

00:17:35.680 --> 00:17:37.910
Skull Juggler's Soulcharge!

00:17:38.710 --> 00:17:40.580
Skull Juggler boosts!

00:17:40.720 --> 00:17:42.630
Mirror Demon attacks!

00:17:47.030 --> 00:17:48.880
Damage trigger check!

00:17:49.250 --> 00:17:50.830
Critical trigger!

00:17:50.830 --> 00:17:53.020
I give all the effects to 
Goddess of the Half Moon!

00:17:56.230 --> 00:17:58.370
Turquoise, if you would...

00:18:01.480 --> 00:18:02.670
No guard!

00:18:03.640 --> 00:18:05.520
Drive trigger check.

00:18:08.980 --> 00:18:10.790
Damage trigger check.

00:18:11.530 --> 00:18:15.650
I'll close the curtain for now, 
having delivered 2 damage.

00:18:15.650 --> 00:18:21.260
I hope the whole audience is looking forward 
to the third act, which will begin shortly.

00:18:24.790 --> 00:18:26.110
Ren...

00:18:27.780 --> 00:18:29.880
I stand and draw!

00:18:30.130 --> 00:18:32.000
Goddess of the Half Moon's skill!

00:18:37.160 --> 00:18:38.670
Oh, no...

00:18:40.290 --> 00:18:42.510
You didn't find it this time, either?

00:18:42.510 --> 00:18:44.150
This isn't your lucky day.

00:18:44.150 --> 00:18:48.060
Luck? I don't rely on that when I'm fighting!

00:18:48.270 --> 00:18:52.720
What's that, acting tough? I figured you 
more for the heart-on-the-sleeve type.

00:18:53.390 --> 00:18:56.300
Wrong. I'm not acting tough.

00:18:56.300 --> 00:18:58.320
I just have faith...

00:18:58.320 --> 00:19:01.910
Faith in this deck and my own ability!

00:19:03.000 --> 00:19:05.410
Shine brightly, beautiful goddess!

00:19:05.650 --> 00:19:08.850
I ride CEO Amaterasu!

00:19:11.020 --> 00:19:12.170
Soulcharge!

00:19:13.970 --> 00:19:16.300
I check the top card of my deck.

00:19:17.290 --> 00:19:19.670
I return this card to the bottom of my deck.

00:19:20.530 --> 00:19:23.430
I call Oracle Guardian, Red Eye!

00:19:26.130 --> 00:19:28.100
I attack Mirror Demon!

00:19:28.740 --> 00:19:31.140
She's attacking the rear-guard?

00:19:33.090 --> 00:19:35.460
I see. That's how she's coming at me...

00:19:35.600 --> 00:19:38.280
In that case, I defend with Big League Bear!

00:19:42.800 --> 00:19:45.180
I activate Big League Bear's skill!

00:19:45.180 --> 00:19:46.520
Soulcharge!

00:19:48.130 --> 00:19:50.880
I attack Mirror Demon with Tagitsuhime!

00:19:51.220 --> 00:19:54.100
There are six Oracle Think 
Tank cards in my Soul,

00:19:54.100 --> 00:19:55.840
so she receives +3000 power!

00:19:56.180 --> 00:19:58.040
Attacking the rear-guard again?

00:19:58.040 --> 00:19:59.340
Why?

00:20:00.700 --> 00:20:04.090
It seems you're afraid 
of Deadly Shadow Beast.

00:20:04.540 --> 00:20:06.560
Deadly Shadow Beast?!

00:20:06.560 --> 00:20:08.850
I see! The card from last time...

00:20:11.160 --> 00:20:14.160
Savage beasts lurk within the 
darkness that is the Soul.

00:20:14.160 --> 00:20:16.480
And there's no way to escape it...

00:20:16.630 --> 00:20:19.340
This secret assassination technique 
of my circus is called:

00:20:19.340 --> 00:20:21.450
Deadly Shadow Beast!

00:20:21.860 --> 00:20:28.410
Every time her attack hits, a new unit will come 
from the Soul, and Misaki's trying to prevent that!

00:20:31.030 --> 00:20:33.780
So you're using what you've 
learned in the past...

00:20:33.890 --> 00:20:37.160
Or is it just that you're 
terrified right now?

00:20:38.180 --> 00:20:39.400
You'll see...

00:20:41.200 --> 00:20:43.520
Fine. No guard.

00:20:48.370 --> 00:20:51.060
I attack Crimson with Amaterasu!

00:20:52.280 --> 00:20:53.430
No guard.

00:20:56.800 --> 00:20:59.270
Twin drive, first check.

00:20:59.460 --> 00:21:00.970
Second check.

00:21:01.350 --> 00:21:04.490
Draw trigger! I give the effect to Amaterasu!

00:21:04.800 --> 00:21:06.450
And then I draw!

00:21:11.070 --> 00:21:12.910
Damage trigger check.

00:21:14.390 --> 00:21:16.370
I have a draw trigger, too.

00:21:16.450 --> 00:21:17.630
Draw.

00:21:20.400 --> 00:21:21.660
Turn end.

00:21:22.440 --> 00:21:24.420
Damage 3-3!

00:21:24.420 --> 00:21:26.230
A tie up to now...

00:21:26.230 --> 00:21:27.850
Misaki...

00:21:28.240 --> 00:21:33.040
Yes. It's a very good fight, 
don't you think, Tetsu?

00:21:33.170 --> 00:21:33.980
No.

00:21:34.790 --> 00:21:36.060
Oh?

00:21:36.480 --> 00:21:38.640
Certainly, in terms of damage, it's a tie.

00:21:38.640 --> 00:21:41.460
And Deadly Shadow Beast has been blocked.

00:21:41.460 --> 00:21:45.000
But Asaka's fighter nickname is Assassin.

00:21:45.000 --> 00:21:46.950
There's no way it's going to end like this.

00:21:47.320 --> 00:21:50.390
Right. Looks like you have 
a good understanding of it.

00:21:53.600 --> 00:21:54.890
Ren...

00:21:56.770 --> 00:21:59.460
I can feel Ren's expectations of me.

00:21:59.790 --> 00:22:03.300
That's right. The show is 
approaching its climax...

00:22:03.910 --> 00:22:08.550
Misaki Tokura... You don't yet know

00:22:08.550 --> 00:22:11.540
the true terror of my Pale Moon Circus.

00:23:53.330 --> 00:23:56.360
It feels like Misaki is 
fighting matter-of-factly...

00:23:56.360 --> 00:23:58.180
But it's like she's slowly 
and steadily heating up...

00:23:58.180 --> 00:23:59.870
This is definitely a fight worth seeing!

00:23:59.870 --> 00:24:02.930
It feels awkward calling out, 
but... good luck, Misaki!

00:24:02.930 --> 00:24:06.040
Wow! That's awesome! Misaki 
really is incredible!

00:24:06.040 --> 00:24:08.020
Go! Go! Misaki!

00:24:08.020 --> 00:24:12.760
I see. Misaki's image of her fight was 
put together from the very beginning!

00:24:12.870 --> 00:24:14.800
Next time: Lord of the Fight!

00:24:15.090 --> 00:24:17.970
I'm gonna fight my own way, too!
